          "id": "india-foodgrain-record-378mt-2026-11-26",
          "headline": "Govt says India grew a record 378 million tonnes of foodgrain in 2025-26",
          "summary": "Agriculture Minister Shivraj Singh Chouhan said 2025-26 foodgrain output topped 378 million tonnes, about 20.8 million tonnes more than the year before. Rice passed 155 million tonnes and wheat hit a record of nearly 122 million tonnes; pulses rose to about 27.2 million tonnes.",
          "why_it_matters": "Bigger grain stocks help keep food prices, and so retail inflation, in check.",
